### Task 3: Readiness gate

The first tool call must not race XFCE booting. We wait for the X display socket, then probe `cua-driver` for AT-SPI capability. Missing AT-SPI degrades to pixel-only rather than failing, per the spec.

We probe with our own short-lived `cua-driver` child rather than reusing nib's, because nib's driver session is internal and not reachable from our code.

